# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W2 kill-switch drill (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prod-fixes (or of
# a branch that carries it) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from
# this branch by its author. ONE IMAGE FOR THE DRILL: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prodfix-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i "s/tp4-prodfix-1/<tag>/" *.env). A commit of a file the
# image carries (w2_switch.py is one) needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this drill never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

# X0: the card state before the drill: status, a rescan of the topology, an all-four reset. READ: four cards present and healthy, the fabric as measured, no other window driver alive. Stop rule: anything else.
# (the owner stops the node agent and unserves production before it, and restores production after Z, with the cutover pack's own steps.)

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prodfix-1
